@abstract:
Hermeneia is an experimental voking query language for asking what a stored
particular can become under a declared use-model. The current implementation
supports `invoke` end-to-end against a local JSONL seed corpus and the external
`tropecheck` oracle. Vocarium is not yet integrated; the other six voke
operations are recognized but not implemented. This declaration records that
boundary rather than treating design intent as delivered capability.

A 2026-10-03 review replaced scaffold-era purpose text and probes that did not
measure Hermeneia. The current project-specific content is provisional until
the maintainer confirms the policies and priorities below.
@end

## Purpose

Hermeneia is the query layer in the trope stack: Vocarium is intended to store
vokeable particulars, Haec records transformations, and Hermeneia queries a
particular under a declared use-model. It emits Trope IR v0.2 and delegates
grade comparison and the p-sufficiency verdict to `tropecheck`.

The implemented vertical slice is `.hil` parsing → `invoke` planning against
the local JSONL store → Trope IR → `tropecheck` → verdict/witness rendering.
Only `invoke` is implemented. `evoke`, `convoke`, `transvoke`, `provoke`,
`intervoke`, and `revoke` remain recognized-but-unimplemented operations.

## Anti-Purpose

Hermeneia is NOT:

- a truth engine or an automatic interpreter;
- a general-purpose search engine, SQL replacement, or thesaurus;
- Vocarium (the intended store) or Haec (the transformation language);
- a reimplementation of the trope grade algebra owned by `trope-checker`;
- evidence that a source grade or warrant is itself correct;
- a replacement for human interpretation or accountability.

A retrieved or interpretable particular is not automatically licensed. A
p-sufficiency verdict is conditional on the supplied grades, use-model, and
checker result; it is not a claim of semantic truth.

## If In Doubt

Ask before changing a boundary-bearing contract. The sensitive areas are:

- `src/hermeneia-syntax/` — accepted syntax and honest reporting of operations
  that are not implemented;
- `src/hermeneia-ir/` — Trope IR v0.2, the integration contract with the oracle;
- `src/hermeneia-core/` — query planning and the rule that the checker owns the
  grade algebra;
- `.machine_readable/contractiles/` and `.machine_readable/descriptiles/` —
  normative contracts and descriptive evidence; changing only one side is drift;
- `docs/SPEC.adoc`, `EXPLAINME.adoc`, and `README.adoc` — public claims must not
  outrun executable receipts;
- any proposed persistent store, network service, deployment, or destructive
  action. None is authorized by this declaration.

## Committed Next-Actions

### contractile-specialization
- description: Replace the inherited generic contractile clauses with an accurate Hermeneia-specific draft and obtain maintainer ratification
- probe: bash scripts/verify-contractiles.sh
- status: in_progress
- notes: |
    The probe verifies file presence, cross-references, and pinned hashes only.
    It does not establish that the owner agrees with the policy choices or that
    the external contractile CLI executes these declarations. Owner review and
    coaptation receipt regeneration remain outstanding.

## Wishes

### Near Horizon

#### vocarium-store-provider
- description: Replace or complement the local JSONL stub with a real Vocarium StoreProvider without changing query planning
- horizon: near
- status: declared
- notes: Vocarium does not exist as an integrated backend in this repository yet.

### Mid Horizon

#### voke-family-implementation
- description: Implement the remaining recognized voke operations with explicit semantics, tests, and truthful status reporting
- horizon: mid
- status: declared
- notes: Do not mark an operation implemented until its executable path and evidence exist.

#### warrant-aware-revocation
- description: Implement `revoke` over a warrant graph so licence withdrawal is traceable and use-relative
- horizon: mid
- status: declared
- notes: Requires a warrant graph and is not part of the current slice.

### Far Horizon

#### loss-vector-from-oracle
- description: Render the full loss vector only after the checker exposes the required violated-coordinate evidence
- horizon: far
- status: declared
- notes: Do not reconstruct or fabricate the vector in Hermeneia while the oracle CLI omits it.
